### MEDUSA API — Submission requires competition registration
### Use a team belonging to the same organization as an active competition.
### This file tests submission BEFORE registration, then AFTER registration.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@memberEmail = participant@example.com
@password = replace-with-participant-password
@competitionId = 1
@teamId = 1
@challengeId = 1

### 1. Login as a team member
# @name memberLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{memberEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 2. Submit before registering (expected 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{teamId}},
  "flag": "replace-with-test-flag"
}

### 3. Register the team for the competition (expected 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/competitions/{{competitionId}}/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{teamId}}
}

### 4. Submit after registration (expected 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{teamId}},
  "flag": "replace-with-test-flag"
}
